<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  RememBox HTTP daemon LaunchAgent template (2026-07-18, the 2026-07-18
  HTTP-daemon engineering log, internal; EnvironmentVariables/port/KeepAlive
  hardened 2026-08-14, "Review round 1 fixes" section of that log).

  This is a TEMPLATE: the binary path, log directory, and port placeholders
  below (double-underscore delimited, ALL-CAPS) plus the EnvironmentVariables
  dict placeholder are substituted by tool/install-daemon.sh before this
  file is copied to ~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.remembox.daemon.plist. Do not
  load this file directly from its repo path — run tool/install-daemon.sh
  instead. (NOTE for anyone editing this comment: do not spell out the
  EnvironmentVariables placeholder token literally here — install-daemon.sh
  matches it with a line-oriented sed `r`/`d` pair, so a second literal
  occurrence anywhere in this file would be corrupted too.)

  A LaunchAgent does NOT inherit the operator's shell environment, so every
  OBX_MEMORY_* variable the daemon needs (sync URL/credentials, embed model,
  Ollama URL, dims, store dir, ...) must be baked in here at install time as
  a captured snapshot. Daemon config is therefore FROZEN AT INSTALL TIME: to
  change any OBX_MEMORY_* variable for the daemon, export it and re-run
  tool/install-daemon.sh (it re-renders and reloads the LaunchAgent).

  OBX_MEMORY_HTTP_TOKEN (2026-09-07, Fix 1, the 2026-09-07 daemon-auth
  engineering log, internal) rides through this SAME generic
  EnvironmentVariables mechanism —
  no dedicated placeholder needed here: tool/install-daemon.sh resolves/
  generates it and exports it into its own process BEFORE the OBX_MEMORY_*
  capture step runs, so it is captured and baked in exactly like every other
  OBX_MEMORY_* variable. The daemon (lib/src/http_transport.dart
  resolveHttpToken) refuses to start without it.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive: the daemon starts at login and launchd restarts it
  on a genuine crash (SuccessfulExit=false), throttled to at most once every
  ThrottleInterval seconds so a held store lock (see instance_guard.dart)
  cannot hot-loop the process. A deliberate `kill`/SIGTERM that exits 0 does
  NOT trigger a restart. To stop it deliberately, unload it first:
  `launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/io.remembox.daemon`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>io.remembox.daemon</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__REMEMBOX_DIST_BIN__</string>
        <string>--serve=__REMEMBOX_PORT__</string>
    </array>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
__REMEMBOX_ENV_DICT__
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Crashed</key>
        <true/>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>
    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>10</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__REMEMBOX_LOG_DIR__/daemon.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__REMEMBOX_LOG_DIR__/daemon.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
